# youtube-intel-mcp needs no secrets to run: every tool is a pure function
# over data you pass in (no YouTube Data API, no vidIQ, no Gemini call from
# inside this server). This file exists only so the repo follows the same
# .env.example convention as its sibling tools in this series, and as a
# placeholder for anyone who forks this to re-add a live-fetch tool later.
#
# If you do add one, put its key here, never in config.example.yaml or any
# committed file.
# YT_API_KEY=
